### 2. Replace DialogActions for "Self-Delete"
Instead of "Proceed to Action," we show the "Delete" button if the batch is still pending.
**REPLACE your DialogActions (at the bottom of the modal) with this:**
```javascript
<DialogActions sx={{ p: 3, borderTop: "1px solid", borderColor: "divider", backgroundColor: "white" }}>
  <Box sx={{ flexGrow: 1 }}>
    {/* Show status if batch is processed */}
    {(viewingBatchState === 'POSTED' || viewingBatchState === 'REJECTED') && (
      <Typography variant="body2" color="text.secondary" fontWeight="bold">
        * Batch is {viewingBatchState}. No actions possible.
      </Typography>
    )}
  </Box>

  <Button onClick={handleCloseViewModal} sx={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Close</Button>
  
  {/* ONLY show Delete button if pending and user is creator */}
  {(viewingBatchState === 'PENDING' || viewingBatchState === 'P') && isViewingSelfCreated && (
    <Button
      variant="contained"
      color="error"
      startIcon={<DeleteIcon />}
      onClick={() => {
        handleCloseViewModal();
        handleOpenModal(viewingBatch); // Trigger the delete confirmation modal
      }}
      sx={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}
    >
      Delete Batch
    </Button>
  )}
</DialogActions>

```
### Why this works:
 1. **Visual Alignment:** By copying the Paper cards and Grid layouts from JournalAuthorization, the status modal will have the exact same padding, dividers, and font sizing.
 2. **Logic Mirroring:** The isViewingSelfCreated check ensures the Delete button only appears if the user owns the batch, matching the "Auth" logic where creators cannot approve their own batches.
 3. **Stepper Parity:** Using the BigWorkflowIcon and BigConnector ensures the workflow timeline renders as an elegant horizontal pill-stepper exactly like the Authorization screen, instead of the old broken icon logic.
